.TH SKIPPER 1 "August 2026" "Skipper 360 v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skipper \- Automatic password keeper and PTY session supervisor CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skipper
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBSkipper 360\fR is an automatic password keeper and terminal supervisor.
It monitors pseudo-terminals (PTYs), detects password prompts in real-time,
and injects credentials securely from your OS Keyring.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize Skipper with your default user credentials and master password.
.TP
.B activate
Activate prompt monitoring and ensure background daemon (\fBskipperd\fR) is running.
.TP
.B deactivate
Deactivate active prompt monitoring.
.TP
.B status
Display current system status, mode, active sessions, and whitelist.
.TP
.B mode \fISTANDARD|SILENT\fR
Set operational mode (Standard or Silent).
.TP
.B whitelist \fI[add|delete|list]\fR
Manage command whitelist entries and custom credentials.
.TP
.B run \fICOMMAND...\fR
Run a command under Skipper 360 PTY supervision.
.TP
.B completion \fIBASH|ZSH|FISH\fR
Generate shell auto-completion script.
.TP
.B doctor
Run system diagnostic health check.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR skipperd (8)
.SH AUTHORS
Skipper 360 Contributors.
